    "updated_at": "2020-06-22T19:27:40Z",
    "body": "The link, as I already noted, is not to a definition. Here's what it links to: \"Text is allowed inside elements, attribute values, and comments. Extra constraints are placed on what is and what is not allowed in text based on where the text is to be put, as described in the other sections.\" That's not a definition. By contrast, shortly after that link is a link for \"character references\" and clicking that does take the user to a definition. The link for \"text\" says what we can do with text and that what is acceptable as text in one context may not be acceptable in another. If that was meant to be a definition, the vagueness of what is collectively called \"the other sections\" makes it not a definition.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
