    "created_at": "2020-06-22T20:17:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-06-22T20:17:47Z",
    "body": "Generally, a definition can replace the word being defined. For example, \"I like red\" given a definition of red as 'electromagnetism with a wavelength of ~700nm'  can become \"I like electromagnetism with a wavelength of ~700nm\". Since specs tend to be precise, we come to expect precision when we encounter another spec. So, if I was confused, various other users will be, too.\r\n\r\nAs an alternative, you could replace \"text\" with \"free-form entry\", \"unlimited string\", or some such, preferably a term already in use elsewhere in the spec. Calling it \"text\" makes it sound already limited to ASCII or some such, although had you meant ASCII per se then we assume you would have used that term.\r\n\r\nThanks.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
